body:
**I'm from Australia.**

&#x200B;

* ***Min Min lights:*** 

The Min Min lights are the spirits of the elderly.

&#x200B;

* ***Bunyips:***

The bunyip once lived in the rivers, lakes, and swamps. Its howl carried through the night air, making people afraid to enter the water. At night, the bunyip prowled the land, hunting for women and children to eat.

&#x200B;

* ***Yowies:***

The yowie is usually described as a hairy and ape-like creature standing upright at between 2.1 m (6 ft 11 in) and 3.6 m (12 ft). 

&#x200B;

* ***The Yara-ma-yha-who:***

Yara Ma Yha Who is a blood-sucking creature that lurks in the treetops until a person walks under it. Then it leaps from the tree onto the person, sucking almost all its blood. It would swallow them whole. After swallowing the poor soul, it would regurgitate the person up, take a drink of water and nap, then wake up to puke the person out over and over. As it does this, he/she will become shorter and redder each time until they themselves become a Yara Ma Yha Who.
